# Require Approval and Review for Every Change

Applies to **any and all** files in this repository — C, headers, ASM, `Makefile`,
`mk64.ld`, YAML, scripts, docs, and these rule files. No exception for "small",
"obvious", "temporary", or "just a doc".

## Before changing anything

1. State which files you will create, edit, rename, or delete.
2. State what will change and why.
3. Wait for **explicit user approval**.

An approval given for an earlier batch is not approval for this one. Do not create,
edit, rename, or delete a file, and do not add or modify code, before approval.

## After changing anything

Every change is **submitted to the user for review** before it is treated as done:

- Present the full diff of what was actually changed.
- List every file touched, including files added or deleted.
- Do not self-approve, do not report the work complete, and do not begin the next
  batch until the user has reviewed.
- "Go ahead and implement" authorizes the edit. It never waives the review.

If anything was changed that was not approved, say so in the review and offer to revert it.

## Scope

- One approved batch at a time. No unapproved extras bundled in.
- No drive-by refactors, formatting passes, or deletion of code that looks unused.
- Temporary diagnostic code (progress meters, debug pokes) is a change too: approval
  to add, review to remove.
